From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:44:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: mtk_dsi: Stop the engine the bootloader left
 running

On phones the bootloader often leaves DSI scanning out in video mode.
mtk_dsi_poweron() then reprograms timing and the D-PHY under the
running engine, and the first DCS command from the panel's prepare()
waits for a video-mode-done interrupt that a reconfigured engine never
raises, so the first atomic commit stalls (seen on the Zinwa Q25,
MT6789).

Stop the engine and select command mode before enabling it, the state
the rest of the power-on sequence and mtk_dsi_host_transfer() expect.
mtk_output_dsi_enable() selects video mode and restarts it as before.

This follows Roman Vivchar's "drm/mediatek: mtk_dsi: stop engine on
mtk_dsi_poweron" for MT6768 (mt6768-mainline 6d3ec2fbb6e7), whose base
already selects command mode there.

Link: https://github.com/mt6768-mainline/linux/commit/6d3ec2fbb6e7
Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
index cf3e2afe..26de9ee5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -712,6 +712,8 @@ static int mtk_dsi_poweron(struct mtk_dsi *dsi)
 		goto err_disable_engine_clk;
 	}
 
+	mtk_dsi_stop(dsi);
+	mtk_dsi_set_cmd_mode(dsi);
 	mtk_dsi_enable(dsi);
 
 	if (dsi->driver_data->has_shadow_ctl)
